<p>it isn’t always quiet. at kohe in hyderabad, people bustle in and out. friends arguing, young parents trying to have a life, families home after years abroad. i spot more stories there than i could ever write.</p>
<p>but i have come to realise that Bangalore is a city of choices. and people here live like an adult. could that be why, hanging out at cafes alone caught on. it's a choice to be alone and not owe an answer to anyone. <span style="color: #A9452A">what do you think?</span></p>
